    {
      "text": "eighth day they came to circumcise the child, Luke 1:59. eight days … for the circumcising of the child … Jesus, Luke 2:21. Moses … gave unto you circumcision, John 7:22. gave him the covenant of circumcision, Acts 7:8. they that were of the circumcision, Acts 11:2. Except ye be circumcised after the manner of Moses, Acts 15:1. Paul … took and circumcised him, Acts 16:3. saying that they ought not to circumcise their children, Acts 21:21. circumcision verily profiteth, if thou keep the law, Rom. 2:25. what profit is there of circumcision, Rom. 3:1. justify the circumcision by faith, Rom. 3:30. he received the sign of circumcision, Rom. 4:11. Christ was a minister of the circumcision, Rom. 15:8. Circumcision is nothing, and uncircumcision is nothing, 1 Cor. 7:19. neither Titus … was compelled to be circumcised, Gal. 2:3. gospel of the circumcision was unto Peter, Gal. 2:7. neither circumcision availeth any thing, Gal. 5:6 (6:15). Gentiles … who are called Uncircumcision, Eph. 2:11. For we are the circumcision, Philip. 3:3. there is neither … circumcision nor uncircumcision, Col. 3:11. who are of the circumcision, Col. 4:11. many unruly and vain … of the circumcision, Titus 1:10.",
